  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trauma Programme- ARCT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARCT is the Rwandese association of trauma counsellors created in 1998. It aims to contribute towards the rehabilitation of victims of trauma in order to facilitate their reintegration in society and consequently prompt their participation in the reconstruction of Rwanda. In the Psychosocial programme, ARCT is considered by CAFOD as a resource partner. Being the first trauma service provider in the country in terms of training and trauma counselling, it helps CAFOD partners by building their capacities in Trainings and supervision of counsellors. In 2008, trainings and refresher courses will continue for mental health professionals from CAFOD partners on various topics such as: trauma and AIDS, trauma and other chronic illnesses, etc and how take care of such a kind of trauma, trauma healing fourteen years after genocide, etc.  The advocacy work will continue through a second training on advocacy, meetings and conferences, media and sensitization of local authorities.</narrative>
  </description>
